## How Tic-Tac-Toe works
// The Tic-Tac-Toe example is the paper game:  X and O take turns, and three in a row wins.
// Its rules fit in three ideas:
// - each square knows its own mark, and draws itself as a button
// - the game knows whose turn it is
// - after each move, the game checks every line of three for a winner
//
// This guide is the same game with one thing missing:  it only checks the ROWS, across.
// Three down, or corner to corner, doesn't win yet.  Adding those is your move, at the end.


## A square:  empty, or holding an X or an O
// "drawable" means each square shows itself on the page, here as a button
a "square" is a drawable thing where:
	- its "mark" is text
	- it "is empty" if its mark is ""
	// a click plays it
	- to draw it:
		return <button part="mark" onClick={play it}>{its mark}</button>

// the board:  nine squares, three a row -- how they look is in styles.css, the other file in this guide
a "board" is a drawable list of squares
a square belongs to one board


## The game
tic tac toe is an app where:
	- its "board" is a new board
	// whose turn it is:  X or O
	- its "turn" is text
	// who won:  X or O, or "" while the game goes on
	- its "winner" is text

	- its "message" is:
		its turn + " to play" if its winner is ""
		its winner + " wins!" otherwise

	// nine empty squares, made with the game
	- to create it:
		repeat 9 times
			add a new square to the board of tic tac toe

	// an empty board, X to play
	- to start a new game:
		for each square in its board
			set the mark of the square to ""
		set its turn to "X"
		set its winner to ""

	// the same mark in all three squares wins
	// - squares are counted 1 to 9, left to right, then down:  1 2 3 is the top row
	- to check the line from square (a as a number) through (b as a number) to (c as a number):
		set mark to the mark of square a of its board
		if mark is "" return
		if the mark of square b of its board is mark and the mark of square c of its board is mark
			set its winner to mark

	// only the three rows, for now
	- to check for a winner:
		check the line from square 1 through 2 to 3
		check the line from square 4 through 5 to 6
		check the line from square 7 through 8 to 9

	- to draw it:
		return <div class="TicTacToe">
			<h2>{its message}</h2>
			{draw its board}
		</div>


## Playing a square
// Nothing happens if someone has won, or the square is taken.
// Otherwise:  the mark goes in, the game checks for a winner, and the turn passes to the other player.
to play (a square):
	if the winner of tic tac toe is not "" or the square is not empty return
	set the mark of the square to the turn of tic tac toe
	check for a winner
	set the turn of tic tac toe to "O" if the turn of tic tac toe is "X" otherwise "X"


## Start
start a new game
start tic tac toe


## A check:  X wins across the top
// It plays a whole game, X in squares 1, 2 and 3, then clears the board for you.
to test a row
	start a new game
	play square 1 of the board of tic tac toe
	play square 4 of the board of tic tac toe
	play square 2 of the board of tic tac toe
	play square 5 of the board of tic tac toe
	play square 3 of the board of tic tac toe
	the message of tic tac toe should be "X wins!"
	start a new game


## Try it
// - Play a game on the right.  Win across the top, and the line above the board says so.
// - Click ↻, above the game, for a fresh board.
//   Now win DOWN the left side:  squares 1, 4 and 7.  Nothing happens.
